  <Properties>
    <mediaPropertyAltText>
      <Value><![CDATA[The plain three-storey red-brick frontage of The Workhouse at Southwell, with rows of small evenly-spaced sash windows and a central entrance, set behind a low garden wall.]]></Value>
    </mediaPropertyAltText>
    <mediaPropertyCountry>
      <Value><![CDATA[[
  "United Kingdom"
]]]></Value>
    </mediaPropertyCountry>
    <mediaPropertyDescription>
      <Value><![CDATA[Built in 1824 as a place of last resort for the destitute, this is the most complete workhouse in existence. Its architecture was influenced by prison design and its harsh regime became a blueprint for workhouses throughout the country.]]></Value>
    </mediaPropertyDescription>
